# Keep the working copy byte-identical to what CI checks out. core.autocrlf gives this Windows
# working copy CRLF while the Linux runner checks out LF, so Prettier's endOfLine default fails
# locally on files that pass in CI.
#
# It is not only a formatter question here. deploy/ holds a systemd unit that is copied to a box,
# and this repository's files were carrying CRLF: when the log-shipping rig was moved out to the
# infrastructure repository, all five files arrived with \r and its CRLF gate rejected them. A
# unit file with \r is bad enough; a script whose shebang reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` does not
# execute at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# gradlew.bat is stored exactly as committed, with no conversion. cmd.exe misreads a batch file's
# labels and goto targets under LF, so it has to reach every working copy with CRLF, and it is
# committed with CRLF: Dependabot's wrapper bumps write it that way. Converting it, as
# `text eol=crlf` did, disagreed with those blobs, and every Windows clone showed it as modified.
*.bat -text
*.jar binary
